Mitcad's patch to OCCT 8.0.1, under OCCT's licence:
SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.1-only WITH OCCT-exception-1.0

Fillets: a rounding of a wall's outer top edge with a radius wider than
the wall's top, the top closed off at the edge's end by a sloping face
(the end's top edge chamfered), takes the top away, its ball rolling on
the inner wall's top edge, and the slope cuts it past the edge's end
(mitcad#1987).

- StartSolOverflow: a side of a convex edge's rounding (its ball inside
  the solid) that went over a face its ball touches at no point, at least
  the radius wide (the inner wall), across an edge where the solid turns
  away by a right angle or more, rolls on that edge instead of touching a
  face beyond (the floor at the inner wall's foot), where a ball touching
  the outer wall and the floor from below took the whole wall away: a
  valid body that was wrong (radii between 2 and 3 on a top 2 wide).
  Past a sliver, and for a concave edge's rounding, nothing changes.
- RolledOnProlongedEdgeAtEnd: a piece ending at the spine's end with its
  contact on the other face inside that face, on no edge and off the
  surfaces of the other faces at the end vertex (the slope cuts it further
  on), rolls on past the end too. Its walk past Er's end rolls on the strip
  of Er's other face (the top's plane) where the ball reaches into B (the
  inner wall) and not into that face; its curve is then moved onto B's
  surface with the guide's parameters, and its transition on B is P's.
- PerformOneCorner: such an end at a vertex whose edges are all convex
  (AllSame) is the cap of ChFi3d_RolledPastEdgeVertex too; the face at the
  end keeps the side of the cap away from the vertex. A cap leaving that
  face (the other contact running past the face's far edge, radii over
  about 3.5 there) is refused in words rather than made invalid.

Upstream: new.

